
// Nested oneof: the outer's first branch is itself a oneof whose last branch (@b)
// partially pulls 30. The outer sees that's short of the full 100, rolls the
// inner pull back, and takes everything from @c. Only @c posts — which requires
// the outer restore to undo funds pulled through the inner oneof (independent
// snapshot marks).
send [GEM 100] (
  source = oneof {
    oneof {
      @a
      @b
    }
    @c
  }
  destination = @dest
)
